# The release publishes with NPM_TOKEN, which direnv loads from the gitignored .env.local (see
# .envrc). Only the reference lives here — npm expands ${NPM_TOKEN} from the environment — so this
# file is safe to commit and there is no second place a token could be left lying around.
#
# It is a granular token scoped to the jira-fetch packages, which is also why publishing needs no
# one-time code: JIRA_FETCH_NPM_OTP stays supported for a plain login, but is not the normal path.
# scripts/publish.ts refuses to start when NPM_TOKEN is unset, because npm would otherwise send the
# literal string "${NPM_TOKEN}" and fail with an unauthorised error that says nothing useful.
//registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken=${NPM_TOKEN}
